    "design": "Identical scene, seeds, variants, and frozen LLM protocol to the v5 50-seed no-occlusion ablation (protocol ablation-v2-type-observable-df-cutin-key-no-occlusion-50-v5-20261023). The only change is the prompt version: relative_evidence_v6b, which makes style recognition position-invariant, uses ego-relative speed bands for leaderless vehicles, and defines the relative_speed sign. CutinEnv native road, dense lane-0 traffic, independent random native type labels; the nearest native vehicle behind the ego is the key and its speed/response follow its native label (Aggressive 10.5 m/s and accelerates, Normal cooperative IDM, Cautious yields). No occlusion: the key is in the first synchronous observation for all 50 seeds. Other lane-0 vehicles within [-40,+250] m are removed; outside traffic and labels remain native. Ego starts in lane 1 at 7 m/s, must cut in to lane 0, and completes at x>=310 m. Only Full Model and Uniform Belief are run. No controller, reward, or scene change; the key response is type-scripted and variant-independent.",
